<div><span class="lens-idx">01 · Groove</span><h2 class="lens-title">Pulse and phrasing</h2></div>
</div>
<p class="lens-idea"><strong>The musical idea:</strong> A pulse is the steady beat you can keep. Rhythmic placement is where a phrase puts its sounds in relation to that beat—on it, before it, after it, or between its main points.</p>
<p class="lens-builds"><strong>How musicians use it:</strong> Musicians create groove collectively through pulse, subdivision, accent, articulation, repetition, and timing. A phrase can lean around the beat while the ensemble keeps the time feel coherent.</p>
<p class="lens-q"><em>What remains steady, and how does the phrase move around it?</em></p>
<p class="lens-cue">First hear melody attacks meet the pulse. Then hear the same pulse continue while the phrase places its energy in the surrounding spaces.</p>
<div class="realmusic viz-embed">
<div class="realmusic-head"><span class="rm-tag">Isolate the relationship</span><span class="rm-work">Melody on the pulse · melody leaning around it</span></div>
<p class="rm-intro">First hear melody attacks meet the pulse. Then hear the same pulse continue while the phrase places its energy in the surrounding spaces.</p>
