<div><span class="lens-idx">02 · Dialogue</span><h2 class="lens-title">Call, response, and exchange</h2></div>
</div>
<p class="lens-idea"><strong>The musical idea:</strong> In call-and-response, one voice or group makes a statement and another answers by echoing, completing, contrasting, interrupting, or commenting on it.</p>
<p class="lens-builds"><strong>How musicians use it:</strong> The relationship between statements creates form and meaning: the response can preserve the first voice, redirect it, or expand the exchange into a group event.</p>
<p class="lens-q"><em>Who begins, who answers, and how does the answer change the statement?</em></p>
<p class="lens-cue">Hear one instrumental voice call and another answer; then hear the exchange grow into a collective return.</p>
